  {"type": "whatis", "img": "/Assets/service/what-is-trauma-ptsd.webp", "alt": "Compassionate, trauma-informed care at Hopewell Health Solutions, Connecticut", "h2": "What is trauma & PTSD?", "paras": ["Trauma is the emotional response to a deeply distressing or disturbing event, whether a single incident or harm that built up over time. Most people recover with support, but for some, the mind and body stay locked in survival mode long after the danger has passed. When symptoms persist for more than a month and interfere with daily life, it may be post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD).", "PTSD isn’t a sign of weakness, and it isn’t “all in your head”, it’s the nervous system’s response to overwhelming experience, and it’s very treatable. The trauma-informed team at Hopewell Health Solutions uses evidence-based therapies like <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/treatment-methods/emdr/\">EMDR</a>, ART, and CPT, along with specialized <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/treatment-methods/group-therapy/\">group programs</a> and medication management, to help you process what happened and feel safe in your life again.", "Trauma can come from a single event, such as an accident, an assault or a sudden loss, or from long-term experiences like abuse, <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/post/recovering-from-narcissistic-abuse-when-therapy-alone-isnt-enough/\">relationship trauma such as narcissistic abuse</a>, or the job-related trauma that <a class=\"inl\" href=\"/programs/first-responder-iop/\">first responders</a> carry."]},
